WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.866 --> 00:00:06.300
Vanillish.

2
00:00:06.366 --> 00:00:09.900
Vanilluxe. Vanill!

3
00:00:09.966 --> 00:00:13.733
- Vanillish! Vanill!
- Vanill! Vanill!

4
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:19.366
Nill!

5
00:00:23.566 --> 00:00:25.133
We're here!

6
00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:31.533
-Pika!

7
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:34.566
Our heroes have finally arrived in Coumarine City,

8
00:00:34.633 --> 00:00:38.066
site of Ash's next Gym Battle, and excitement abounds.

9
00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:42.000
With its mild climate, Coumarine City is famous as a resort spot.

10
00:00:42.066 --> 00:00:44.933
Ah! Gym Battle, here I come.

11
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:47.666
And the Pokémon Showcase. All right!

12
00:00:47.733 --> 00:00:50.066
You two are really ready. Awesome.

13
00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:52.833
You bet. Let's race to the Pokémon Centre.

14
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:56.500
-Do we have to race? Ugh.

15
00:01:00.433 --> 00:01:03.400
Huh? Hey, guys, can we get some ice cream, please?

16
00:01:03.466 --> 00:01:04.933
Pika.

17
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.833
There you go.

18
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:10.233
Aw, cute, and it's shaped like a Vanillite.

19
00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:11.666
Yep, it is.

20
00:01:11.733 --> 00:01:15.600
That's because there's a lost Vanillite being taken care of in town.

21
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:18.866
It's so adorable. It's become quite popular.

22
00:01:18.933 --> 00:01:23.500
- I thought an item like this would be fun.
- I wanna see Vanillite. Please.

23
00:01:23.566 --> 00:01:24.733
Denne-ne!

24
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.566
- It's at the Pokémon Centre.
- Wow!

25
00:01:26.633 --> 00:01:29.333
I'm sure Nurse Joy would be more than happy to let you.

26
00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:31.166
I'd like to see the Vanillite too!

27
00:01:31.233 --> 00:01:35.933
- Sounds good. Let's check it out.
- Yippee!

28
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.400
Wow, Vanillite ice cream. Yum.

29
00:01:39.466 --> 00:01:41.300
I wanna big slurp too.

30
00:01:41.366 --> 00:01:43.900
Hey, I know just what we'll do.

31
00:01:43.966 --> 00:01:46.266
First, let's... And then...

32
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

33
00:01:49.866 --> 00:01:51.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

34
00:01:51.633 --> 00:01:55.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

35
00:01:55.066 --> 00:01:56.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

36
00:01:56.533 --> 00:02:00.500
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

37
00:02:00.566 --> 00:02:03.633
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

38
00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.500
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

39
00:02:06.566 --> 00:02:11.033
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

40
00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:15.733
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

41
00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.000
♪ Pokémon! ♪

42
00:02:20.966 --> 00:02:23.833
Thawing an Icy Panic!

43
00:02:36.500 --> 00:02:40.000
- Wow.
- Coumarine City has so many Grass types!

44
00:02:40.066 --> 00:02:43.166
Vileplume and Jumpluff and Budew too!

45
00:02:43.233 --> 00:02:44.966
- Wow, an Exeggutor.
- Exeggutor.

46
00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:47.733
Ha, ha. Bellossom!

47
00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:51.266
Chespin, Che!

48
00:02:51.866 --> 00:02:54.333
Che! -Bel.

49
00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:56.166
- Bello!
- Che.

50
00:02:56.233 --> 00:02:59.500
- Chespin strikes out again.
- Ah, I know!

51
00:02:59.566 --> 00:03:03.300
'Scuse me, you're a keeper. Won't you please take care of my brother?

52
00:03:03.366 --> 00:03:04.800
Huh?

53
00:03:06.166 --> 00:03:07.133
Uh-oh.

54
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:10.333
Bonnie, I told you not to do this a million times.

55
00:03:10.400 --> 00:03:12.633
So please think about it, OK?

56
00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.366
Whoa, this is pretty steep.

57
00:03:22.433 --> 00:03:26.633
I wonder if all the people who live around here climb these hills every single day.

58
00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:29.400
Come on, hurry. Clemont, you too!

59
00:03:29.466 --> 00:03:31.633
I'm doing my best.

60
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:32.900
-Huh?

61
00:03:36.966 --> 00:03:39.700
- Hey, was that...
- A monorail.

62
00:03:39.766 --> 00:03:42.966
- Nenne.
- Wow! A monorail? I wanna ride it.

63
00:03:43.033 --> 00:03:45.266
It looks like it goes to the top of this hill.

64
00:03:45.333 --> 00:03:47.766
I wish someone woulda told me that earlier.

65
00:03:47.833 --> 00:03:52.133
Well, we can't just turn back now.

66
00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.766
A-ha, I should have used this right from the start.

67
00:03:55.833 --> 00:03:58.133
The future is now, thanks to science.

68
00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:01.000
Clemontic Gear, on.

69
00:04:01.066 --> 00:04:03.200
My Easy-Peasy Mountain Climber.

70
00:04:03.266 --> 00:04:06.366
The perfect device for making any incline super-easy

71
00:04:06.433 --> 00:04:09.366
and 100 per cent effortless to climb!

72
00:04:09.433 --> 00:04:11.866
All right. Ready? Power on.

73
00:04:13.933 --> 00:04:16.200
- Pika!
- Wow, science is so amazing.

74
00:04:16.266 --> 00:04:19.166
Come on, Clemont, that's not fair.

75
00:04:19.233 --> 00:04:21.533
Uh, oh. No!

76
00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.600
- Hey, Clemont, what's wrong?
- Pika.

77
00:04:23.666 --> 00:04:28.833
- Aah! Ugh! It's out of control!
- Where are you going? Clemont?

78
00:04:33.900 --> 00:04:35.633
Clemont, are you OK?

79
00:04:35.700 --> 00:04:38.833
I guess it needs a little more research and development.

80
00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.933
Huh?

81
00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:43.500
- Huh?

82
00:04:43.566 --> 00:04:48.233
- A bunch of Victreebel.
- Ah, wait, wait! Aah!

83
00:04:48.300 --> 00:04:50.700
Why does Clemont have all the fun?

84
00:04:50.766 --> 00:04:54.100
- I wanna get tickled too.
- Bonnie, hold on!

85
00:04:54.166 --> 00:04:56.466
I think the Victreebel are mad. Hm?

86
00:04:56.533 --> 00:04:58.800
-Clemont's in trouble.

87
00:04:58.866 --> 00:05:01.466
- Help him, Ash.
- Pikachu, use Thunderbolt.

88
00:05:01.533 --> 00:05:04.766
Pika, Pikachu!

89
00:05:06.966 --> 00:05:08.266
Oof!

90
00:05:08.333 --> 00:05:11.133
-Oh, no. Clemont, are you OK?

91
00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.766
Uh. Yeah. I think so.

92
00:05:14.066 --> 00:05:17.900
- I think the Victreebel are still mad.
- Pikachu.

93
00:05:21.566 --> 00:05:22.733
- Pika.
- Whoa.

94
00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:24.533
What are you whippersnappers doin'?

95
00:05:24.600 --> 00:05:28.033
This place is strictly off-limits to the general public.

96
00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:29.766
Uh, sorry.

97
00:05:29.833 --> 00:05:32.133
- We didn't know.
- I'm sorry, sir.

98
00:05:32.200 --> 00:05:34.766
This is all because my invention went haywire.

99
00:05:34.833 --> 00:05:37.766
It broke the fence and I ended up here.

100
00:05:37.833 --> 00:05:42.500
Hm. Yes, I imagine all the Victreebel were mighty spooked.

101
00:05:42.566 --> 00:05:45.000
- Aww.
- Victreebel? We're really sorry.

102
00:05:48.066 --> 00:05:52.100
Uh, sir? Will you tell us why this place is off-limits?

103
00:05:52.166 --> 00:05:56.000
Yes, of course. This area is a pasture for Grass types.

104
00:05:59.066 --> 00:06:02.566
So I guess you watch over all those grazing Pokémon.

105
00:06:02.633 --> 00:06:06.433
Yep. Truth is, this ranch belongs to me.

106
00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:09.033
Grass-type Pokémon are just wonderful.

107
00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.566
And Gogoat? It's a Grass type too.

108
00:06:11.633 --> 00:06:13.466
Aah!

109
00:06:15.466 --> 00:06:19.600
Gogoat. The Mount Pokémon and the evolved form of Skiddo.

110
00:06:19.666 --> 00:06:21.966
Gogoat is able to sense its trainer's feelings

111
00:06:22.033 --> 00:06:25.066
by detecting small changes in the grip on its horns.

112
00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:29.100
This allows both trainer and Pokémon to move together as one.

113
00:06:29.166 --> 00:06:31.533
That's right, and look.

114
00:06:31.600 --> 00:06:33.833
Those are all my Sunflora over there.

115
00:06:33.900 --> 00:06:39.333
By usin' the power of their Solar Beams, I can generate electricity.

116
00:06:39.400 --> 00:06:42.133
- Pika!
- The future is now, thanks to science.

117
00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:45.566
- That's simply incredible.
- Your ranch is so cool.

118
00:06:45.633 --> 00:06:48.066
Guess so.

119
00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:51.266
Tell me, where are you all headed, anyway?

120
00:06:51.333 --> 00:06:52.566
To the Pokémon Centre.

121
00:06:52.633 --> 00:06:57.233
Well, in that case, there's a short cut that runs right through my ranch.

122
00:06:57.300 --> 00:07:00.566
If you take it, you'll be there in no time.

123
00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:05.866
That joint's where the lost Vanillite's being taken care of.

124
00:07:05.933 --> 00:07:10.533
We'll grab it as planned and then use its cold air to make Vanillite ice cream.

125
00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.866
We'll sell tons of that tasty treat and we'll make a fortune.

126
00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:16.866
And then the Boss'll give us another fortune.

127
00:07:16.933 --> 00:07:18.233
Let's not wait another sec.

128
00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:20.200
Hi, Pokémon Centre!

129
00:07:20.266 --> 00:07:21.366
We're here!

130
00:07:22.400 --> 00:07:25.000
Vanillite! Vanillite!

131
00:07:26.433 --> 00:07:29.366
- Excuse us, Nurse Joy.
- Yes, can I help you?

132
00:07:29.433 --> 00:07:30.733
Wigglytuff.

133
00:07:30.800 --> 00:07:34.233
Are you taking care of a Vanillite here at the Pokémon Centre?

134
00:07:34.300 --> 00:07:38.000
That's right. There's a Vanillite here.

135
00:07:38.066 --> 00:07:41.466
- Could we possibly meet Vanillite?
- Please, oh, please, oh, please?

136
00:07:41.533 --> 00:07:45.466
- Sure. Of course.
- Wigglytuff. Tuff, Wigglytuff.

137
00:07:45.533 --> 00:07:49.966
You see, at the moment, Vanillite is being kept in a cooled room.

138
00:07:50.033 --> 00:07:53.100
Ah, where? Is Vanillite in there?

139
00:07:53.166 --> 00:07:55.333
Come this way.

140
00:07:55.400 --> 00:07:58.633
Vanillite, come on out and say hi.

141
00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:00.600
Nilla?

142
00:08:00.666 --> 00:08:02.166
Vanillite!

143
00:08:02.233 --> 00:08:06.000
- It's nice to meet you.
- Vanillite's very friendly.

144
00:08:06.066 --> 00:08:08.666
- Vanillite! Ah! Vanill!
- Aww. You feel so cold!

145
00:08:09.766 --> 00:08:11.733
-Vanillite!

146
00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.233
Vanillite. The Fresh Snow Pokémon.

147
00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:18.366
Vanillite is created from ice crystals that are illuminated by the morning sun.

148
00:08:18.433 --> 00:08:20.766
Its breath is 58 degrees below zero.

149
00:08:20.833 --> 00:08:23.766
If you get a little too close, you're gonna freeze.

150
00:08:23.833 --> 00:08:27.500
- I guess you're right.
- Denne!

151
00:08:27.566 --> 00:08:28.800
-Vanillite!

152
00:08:28.866 --> 00:08:32.933
I can see why it's so popular that they even named an ice cream after it.

153
00:08:33.000 --> 00:08:34.500
Vanillite's so cute.

154
00:08:34.566 --> 00:08:38.700
But I would imagine that Vanillite's friends and family are worried by now.

155
00:08:38.766 --> 00:08:41.066
- I'm sure it's very lonely as well.
- Pikachu!

156
00:08:41.133 --> 00:08:43.433
We'll have to bring Vanillite back to the mountain

157
00:08:43.500 --> 00:08:45.500
once it's gotten its strength back.

158
00:08:45.566 --> 00:08:47.133
Vanillite.

159
00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.500
Denne-ne-ne!

160
00:08:48.566 --> 00:08:51.266
Uh-oh. It looks like you're hungry already.

161
00:08:51.333 --> 00:08:52.766
Vanillite!

162
00:08:52.833 --> 00:08:56.766
- OK. I'll go and get lunch prepared.
- Wigglytuff.

163
00:08:56.833 --> 00:09:00.300
I wanna help feed Vanillite too!

164
00:09:00.366 --> 00:09:03.733
- Would it be all right if we assisted you?
- That would be great.

165
00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:05.966
- Why don't you come with me?
- Yay!

166
00:09:06.033 --> 00:09:08.300
- This is gonna be awesome.
- Denne-ne!

167
00:09:08.366 --> 00:09:09.833
Don't you think so, buddy?

168
00:09:09.900 --> 00:09:12.600
Va?

169
00:09:14.066 --> 00:09:15.066
Oh?

170
00:09:15.133 --> 00:09:16.433
Nil!

171
00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:19.933
Ash, would you take a bottle down from the shelf?

172
00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:23.900
- Uh, how about this one?
- I wanna do it! I wanna do it!

173
00:09:23.966 --> 00:09:26.433
Ah! Hm. Ah!

174
00:09:28.366 --> 00:09:30.766
Cute little Vanillite, lunch is ready!

175
00:09:30.833 --> 00:09:32.900
And I promise you it'll be delectable.

176
00:09:32.966 --> 00:09:35.866
Vanill! Nillite!

177
00:09:35.933 --> 00:09:37.200
Vanillite!

178
00:09:37.266 --> 00:09:41.233
-Here's your very own talking lunch!

179
00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:42.433
Boxed and ready!

180
00:09:44.900 --> 00:09:47.066
- Excuse us.
- Coming through!

181
00:09:47.133 --> 00:09:50.566
- Whoa, hey. Watch out.
- Oh, no!

182
00:09:50.633 --> 00:09:53.200
- Vanillite's not there.
- Not there?

183
00:09:53.266 --> 00:09:56.233
- I wonder if it could be...
- Yeah, it was those three.

184
00:09:57.333 --> 00:09:59.833
Uh, there they are. Come back!

185
00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.833
Quick, Nurse Joy, call Officer Jenny.

186
00:10:01.900 --> 00:10:03.233
- All right!
- Thanks!

187
00:10:05.800 --> 00:10:07.366
Vanillite!

188
00:10:07.433 --> 00:10:09.600
Hey, keep a lid on it, ice head.

189
00:10:14.366 --> 00:10:17.333
Vanill!

190
00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:26.200
Who's that Pokémon?

191
00:10:28.066 --> 00:10:30.100
It's Vanillite!

192
00:10:30.166 --> 00:10:32.166
Vanillite!

193
00:10:43.066 --> 00:10:45.666
- Freezing!

194
00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:49.433
Folks, everybody get inside. And hurry!

195
00:10:49.500 --> 00:10:52.733
Excuse me, Ramos, what's going on?

196
00:10:52.800 --> 00:10:53.666
Hm.

197
00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:04.533
- Why is it snowing?
- Pika. Pika.

198
00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:05.700
I'm so cold.

199
00:11:05.766 --> 00:11:08.900
What could've happened to cause a sudden blizzard like this?

200
00:11:08.966 --> 00:11:11.100
It was so warm a minute ago.

201
00:11:11.166 --> 00:11:14.300
Over there! It's them!

202
00:11:14.366 --> 00:11:18.033
On second thought, I think I'll pass on that ice cream in this weather.

203
00:11:18.100 --> 00:11:20.800
- Vanillite! Vanillite!
- Cool it! So to speak.

204
00:11:20.866 --> 00:11:25.033
- All right, you guys, come back here.
- Huh?

205
00:11:27.166 --> 00:11:29.766
Prepare for trouble, giving orders like that!

206
00:11:29.833 --> 00:11:32.033
We'll take no lip from a flash-frozen brat!

207
00:11:32.100 --> 00:11:34.600
To protect the world from sticky fingers!

208
00:11:34.666 --> 00:11:37.333
To unite forces while the twerpish threat lingers!

209
00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:40.433
To denounce the mistreatment of Vanillite thieves!

210
00:11:40.500 --> 00:11:43.900
Dealing with you twerps is one of my pet peeves!

211
00:11:43.966 --> 00:11:45.600
- Jessie!
- And James.

212
00:11:45.666 --> 00:11:49.600
Team Rocket fairly freezes with our newly found Vanillite...

213
00:11:49.666 --> 00:11:54.666
Surrender now or prepare for an icicle fight... Brr!

214
00:11:54.733 --> 00:11:58.066
- This weather's not right!
- Not you guys again!

215
00:11:58.133 --> 00:12:00.566
What are you planning to do with Vanillite?

216
00:12:00.633 --> 00:12:03.966
Keep your frozen nose out of other people's business!

217
00:12:04.033 --> 00:12:06.700
-Who turned down the thermostat?

218
00:12:06.766 --> 00:12:08.233
Ah, did they?

219
00:12:08.300 --> 00:12:12.233
- Vanillish!
- Vanilluxe!

220
00:12:12.300 --> 00:12:13.466
-Pika!

221
00:12:13.533 --> 00:12:16.966
Maybe this crazy weather is because of them.

222
00:12:18.366 --> 00:12:22.600
Vanillish. The Icy Snow Pokémon and the evolved form of Vanillite.

223
00:12:22.666 --> 00:12:25.800
Vanillish forms ice particles in the air by cooling it down,

224
00:12:25.866 --> 00:12:27.966
then uses them to freeze opponents.

225
00:12:29.233 --> 00:12:32.833
Vanilluxe. The Snowstorm Pokémon and the evolved form of Vanillish.

226
00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.966
Vanilluxe forms internal clouds of snow by swallowing lots of water

227
00:12:36.033 --> 00:12:37.966
and can cause violent blizzards when angry.

228
00:12:38.033 --> 00:12:41.466
- Vanillite!

229
00:12:43.266 --> 00:12:45.666
-So cold!

230
00:12:45.733 --> 00:12:48.133
Vanillite must've been calling out to those two.

231
00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:51.233
Maybe they're friends of Vanillite. Here to rescue it.

232
00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:53.700
Team Rocket, give Vanillite back right now.

233
00:12:53.766 --> 00:12:55.266
Not a chance.

234
00:12:55.333 --> 00:12:58.700
Not after the freezing work we've done stealing it.

235
00:12:58.766 --> 00:13:00.500
- Nillish!
- Nilluxe!

236
00:13:03.066 --> 00:13:05.633
- Vanillish!
- Vanilluxe!

237
00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:08.966
- Ah!
- Vanillish, Vanilluxe, you've gotta stop!

238
00:13:13.933 --> 00:13:16.066
-Pika!

239
00:13:16.133 --> 00:13:19.900
- Ash, come back!
- It's too dangerous!

240
00:13:19.966 --> 00:13:22.000
Vanillish! Vanilluxe!

241
00:13:22.066 --> 00:13:24.566
- Calm down!
- Pika, pi!

242
00:13:24.633 --> 00:13:28.033
Vanillite. I promise.

243
00:13:29.933 --> 00:13:32.066
- Aah!
- Pika!

244
00:13:32.133 --> 00:13:34.500
-Pika!

245
00:13:34.566 --> 00:13:36.000
- Pika?
- Huh?

246
00:13:37.933 --> 00:13:40.733
Hold on, whippersnapper. You'll freeze.

247
00:13:40.800 --> 00:13:43.000
-All right!

248
00:13:43.066 --> 00:13:44.800
I've gotta stop those two.

249
00:13:44.866 --> 00:13:49.233
Young man, attackin' head-on can be a good thing at times.

250
00:13:49.300 --> 00:13:51.800
Other times, you have to take the side roads.

251
00:13:51.866 --> 00:13:54.300
- Pika?
- The side roads? What do you mean?

252
00:13:54.366 --> 00:13:56.933
Let me demonstrate.

253
00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.566
Now, Jumpluff, go!

254
00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:03.933
- Jump, Jumpluff!
- Jumpluff, Sunny Day!

255
00:14:04.000 --> 00:14:07.666
Jump, Jumpluff!

256
00:14:15.300 --> 00:14:19.566
Good. Now, all my Sunflora, gather together as one.

257
00:14:23.133 --> 00:14:24.800
Sunflora! Sunflora!

258
00:14:24.866 --> 00:14:28.966
- Wow, I've never seen so many Sunflora.
- I wonder what they're gonna do.

259
00:14:29.033 --> 00:14:32.833
Sunflora, I want you to combine forces and use Solar Beam.

260
00:14:32.900 --> 00:14:33.966
Sun!

261
00:14:37.600 --> 00:14:41.166
Sunflora!

262
00:14:50.133 --> 00:14:51.233
- Huh?
- Look!

263
00:14:51.300 --> 00:14:53.566
Vanilluxe and Vanillish are back to normal.

264
00:14:53.633 --> 00:14:57.233
- Great. Thanks, Sunflora!
- Sunflora! Sunflora!

265
00:14:57.300 --> 00:15:01.033
Controlling that many Grass-type Pokémon at the same time.

266
00:15:01.100 --> 00:15:04.033
That guy's incredible.

267
00:15:04.100 --> 00:15:07.633
- Warmth. We thawed out.
- Bein' an ice cube stinks.

268
00:15:07.700 --> 00:15:09.500
All right. Time for Plan B.

269
00:15:09.566 --> 00:15:12.766
- Now that's some thawed thinking.
- Yeah, let's turn up the heat.

270
00:15:12.833 --> 00:15:15.266
With our Fiendish Fever Freeze!

271
00:15:15.333 --> 00:15:18.433
All right!

272
00:15:18.500 --> 00:15:20.633
-Ready for action!

273
00:15:22.866 --> 00:15:24.866
Aah!

274
00:15:24.933 --> 00:15:27.800
First we put all three into the cold collectors,

275
00:15:27.866 --> 00:15:29.866
then we turn it up all the way to ten.

276
00:15:29.933 --> 00:15:32.733
Vanill!

277
00:15:34.800 --> 00:15:36.866
Using their power in such a manner

278
00:15:36.933 --> 00:15:39.833
makes our Plan B almost as good as Plan A.

279
00:15:39.900 --> 00:15:44.266
And our Fiendish Fever Freeze makes making yummy ice cream a breeze!

280
00:15:44.333 --> 00:15:47.166
Time for you to do that thing you do so well.

281
00:15:47.233 --> 00:15:51.000
Give us the juice, so we can whip us up some twerpsicles.

282
00:15:55.166 --> 00:15:57.133
Let me explain.

283
00:15:57.200 --> 00:16:00.666
Our brilliant device sucks up the frigid air emitted by this trio,

284
00:16:00.733 --> 00:16:02.333
making it even colder.

285
00:16:02.400 --> 00:16:03.733
It warms my heart.

286
00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:07.466
Oh, wow. I have to admit that it's very good science.

287
00:16:07.533 --> 00:16:10.733
- What is this, the Team Rocket fan club?
- Dedenne-ne-ne-ne!

288
00:16:10.800 --> 00:16:13.233
We have to do something or we'll freeze.

289
00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:17.266
- Clemont, Serena, let's work together.
- Got it!

290
00:16:17.333 --> 00:16:19.233
We've gotta save Vanillite and the others!

291
00:16:19.300 --> 00:16:22.166
- Luxio, let's go!
- You too, Fennekin!

292
00:16:23.966 --> 00:16:26.733
- Lux!
- Fennekin!

293
00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:29.900
- Pikachu, we've gotta stop that thing!
- Achu.

294
00:16:29.966 --> 00:16:33.133
Bring it. Love it when twerps fail. Wail!

295
00:16:36.100 --> 00:16:38.566
- Pikachu, Thunderbolt, quick!
- Pika!

296
00:16:38.633 --> 00:16:40.466
- Discharge!
- Use Flamethrower!

297
00:16:40.533 --> 00:16:42.166
Pikachu!

298
00:16:42.233 --> 00:16:44.733
Luxio!

299
00:16:44.800 --> 00:16:47.100
Fennekin!

300
00:16:47.166 --> 00:16:48.733
Maxed-out cool!

301
00:16:52.266 --> 00:16:54.266
- I think it stopped!
- Hm.

302
00:16:54.333 --> 00:16:58.033
Now, Meowth, why not grab the entire twerp group?

303
00:16:58.100 --> 00:17:00.333
Hey, why am I the only chump workin'?

304
00:17:04.200 --> 00:17:08.633
I don't like this. Gogoat, use Grass Knot.

305
00:17:12.266 --> 00:17:15.000
- What's going on?
- Something's gone awry.

306
00:17:15.066 --> 00:17:17.400
Uh, looks like we're dead in the ice water.

307
00:17:17.466 --> 00:17:21.833
Excellent job. All right, Gogoat, Leech Seed.

308
00:17:24.800 --> 00:17:25.933
Now's our chance!

309
00:17:26.000 --> 00:17:29.666
We've got to destroy the vent that's been releasing all of that cold air!

310
00:17:29.733 --> 00:17:33.700
OK! Frogadier, I choose you!

311
00:17:34.933 --> 00:17:39.533
- Use Cut on that machine's air vent!
- Frogadier, frog!

312
00:17:43.333 --> 00:17:45.766
- Awesome!
- Yes. Well done!

313
00:17:45.833 --> 00:17:47.866
Vanillite! Vanillite!

314
00:17:47.933 --> 00:17:49.633
- Vanillish!
- Vanilluxe!

315
00:17:54.833 --> 00:17:56.466
-So cold!

316
00:17:57.833 --> 00:18:00.266
Pikachu, use Iron Tail.

317
00:18:00.333 --> 00:18:02.533
Pika, Pika!

318
00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:06.733
- Vanillite!
- Vanilluxe!

319
00:18:12.266 --> 00:18:15.566
All right. All three of you did a totally amazing job!

320
00:18:15.633 --> 00:18:17.300
Pika, pika. Pikachu!

321
00:18:17.366 --> 00:18:21.133
'Kay, Pikachu, use Thunderbolt. Frogadier, you use Water Pulse.

322
00:18:21.200 --> 00:18:24.033
- All right, Luxio, Swift.
- Fennekin, Flamethrower.

323
00:18:24.100 --> 00:18:26.400
Pikachu!

324
00:18:26.466 --> 00:18:28.566
Frogadier!

325
00:18:28.633 --> 00:18:31.033
- Lux!
- Fennekin!

326
00:18:34.100 --> 00:18:36.700
- It's...
- Blast off...

327
00:18:36.766 --> 00:18:39.100
Time!

328
00:18:39.166 --> 00:18:41.433
- All right!
- Lux!

329
00:18:46.066 --> 00:18:48.200
Hm.

330
00:18:51.466 --> 00:18:53.633
- Vanillish!
- Vanilluxe!

331
00:18:55.133 --> 00:18:57.333
- Vanillite!
- Vanilluxe!

332
00:18:57.466 --> 00:19:01.100
I'm so happy that your friends were able to find you, Vanillite.

333
00:19:01.166 --> 00:19:03.333
- Wigglytuff!
- Yeah, bye-bye!

334
00:19:03.400 --> 00:19:04.400
Denne!

335
00:19:04.466 --> 00:19:08.700
And, sir, we owe you a huge debt of gratitude for everything you did.

336
00:19:08.766 --> 00:19:10.633
And the Grass-type Pokémon too.

337
00:19:10.700 --> 00:19:13.866
- Yeah, thank you for everything.
- Pika, pika.

338
00:19:13.933 --> 00:19:16.266
Well, it was nothin'.

339
00:19:16.333 --> 00:19:18.566
- Now, young man.
- Huh?

340
00:19:18.633 --> 00:19:21.833
Life isn't always about travellin' head on.

341
00:19:21.900 --> 00:19:25.100
Sometimes you have to take the side roads instead.

342
00:19:25.166 --> 00:19:27.000
Remember that.

343
00:19:27.066 --> 00:19:28.533
- OK. You bet.
- Pika.

344
00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:31.100
Good.

345
00:19:31.166 --> 00:19:33.466
I like your spirit, son.

346
00:19:33.533 --> 00:19:36.266
Thank you very much, Ramos.

347
00:19:36.333 --> 00:19:39.966
- Where have I heard that name?
- Hi, my name's Serena.

348
00:19:40.033 --> 00:19:43.366
And Bonnie's my name. This is my friend, Dedenne.

349
00:19:43.433 --> 00:19:45.766
- And my big brother.
- I'm Clemont.

350
00:19:45.833 --> 00:19:50.233
- I'm Ash and this is my partner, Pikachu.
- Pikachu!

351
00:19:50.300 --> 00:19:54.000
See, I came here so I could have a battle at the Coumarine City Gym.

352
00:19:54.066 --> 00:19:56.066
Oh, a Gym Battle, eh?

353
00:19:56.133 --> 00:20:00.433
I'm sure the Gym Leader there would be more than happy to accept your challenge.

354
00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:03.466
-Well then, see you again.

355
00:20:03.533 --> 00:20:05.133
Goodbye, sir!

356
00:20:05.200 --> 00:20:07.733
Ne, denne!

357
00:20:07.800 --> 00:20:10.466
- Huh?
- Huh?

358
00:20:10.533 --> 00:20:15.233
That man's a Grass-type Gym Leader.

359
00:20:15.300 --> 00:20:18.333
Yes, I'm the Coumarine Gym Leader.

360
00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.966
I'll be waitin' for ya.

361
00:20:22.866 --> 00:20:25.300
Not only were our heroes able to get past

362
00:20:25.366 --> 00:20:27.566
the disturbing events that gripped Coumarine City,

363
00:20:27.633 --> 00:20:30.300
but also, the powerful Grass-type master who helped them

364
00:20:30.366 --> 00:20:35.033
turned out to be none other than Ramos, the Coumarine City Gym Leader.

365
00:20:35.100 --> 00:20:38.366
The time for Ash's Coumarine City Gym Battle is here,

366
00:20:38.433 --> 00:20:41.433
and we'll soon find out if Ash is able to defeat Ramos

367
00:20:41.500 --> 00:20:47.133
and get his fourth Kalos Gym badge as the journey continues.
